msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:185
#: d4de2be051d147538c8c3fab9a96b888
msgid "The MAVProxy console will then give status information for the Vicon, showing position, attitude and messages rates. The vehicle should also get GPS lock. It will show up at the GPS coordinates in the vicon module settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:191
#: eaf25a963af744d98ff85b7ea136ef89
msgid "Checking Orientations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:193
#: 2b4e69eba7ff49e7ac936abb3cb34726
msgid "Use the Vicon status line in the MAVProxy console to check that you have the right orientation in the data coming from the Vicon. The VPos data is in NED format in meters. The VATT data is euler angles of roll, pitch yaw. Carefully check that these values are consistent while you rotate and move the vehicle before proceeding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:200
#: dceee78ed1a948738385c7438b65df81
msgid "Test Flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:202
#: 8eeca12b85a34b869c2b905d662b7889
msgid "You should see ArduPilot first report that EKF3 gets yaw alignment, and then that it is using the GPS. After that you should be able to arm and fly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:206
#: 5bc9a5cfe3ea45e29685ee6ff1cf3c14
msgid "For a first test flight :ref:`Stabilize mode <stabilize-mode>` or :ref:`Alt Hold mode <altholdmode>` mode is recommended. Then get the flight log from the microSD card and check that the EKF3 innovations are low. The position, velocity and yaw normalised innovations should all be low (below 0.1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:211
#: cb555f60958949399709f005ba39903b
msgid "Once you have confirmed low innovations you can try a flight in :ref:`Loiter mode <loiter-mode>` mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:215
#: 3893d416480c46e39a401fde2d108616
msgid "Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:217
#: b180ccdf68e0456fb77a6c600f637a7f
msgid "If you have significant vibration then you will likely want to de-weight the accelerometers and instead tell the EKF to use the vicon data more. Try setting :ref:`EK3_ACC_P_NSE <EK3_ACC_P_NSE>` to 2.0 to de-weight the accelerometer data. You may find this helps with position and height hold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:223
#: e396f73dfa3e40c082f6a0aa3ac7bf81
msgid "For indoor flight with a Vicon setup and a small quad you can push up the accelerations and yaw rate to much higher value than are used in a normal quad. Some suggestions for a small racing quad are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:227
#: 923533de260b44839199c2d94b6a6629
msgid ":ref:`INS_GYRO_FILTER <INS_GYRO_FILTER>` = 60"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:228
#: ca63b9e2de4741d0811eb641e0d631f6
msgid ":ref:`INS_ACCEL_FILTER <INS_ACCEL_FILTER>` = 30"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:229
#: 7a8c90b790dd4b03a5eeb0802cf71263
msgid ":ref:`ATC_ACC_Y_MAX <ATC_ACC_Y_MAX>` = 100000"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:230
#: 569e14153d454f8190626177c698c868
msgid ":ref:`ATC_RATE_WPY_MAX <ATC_RATE_WPY_MAX>` = 15000"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:233
#: e5fbda653f3b4715a3717899e48b1fdb
msgid "Circle Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:235
#: 2c97aebd20564feb8c0a87b853428c34
msgid "A very useful mode for testing accuracy of flight is :ref:`Circle mode <circle-mode>`. To use it indoors try:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:238
#: ffe8c1c54b6e4573b5295a859ae2182a
msgid ":ref:`CIRCLE_RADIUS_M <CIRCLE_RADIUS_M>` = 100"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:239
#: a9ebddd1187d45dbb9483d1fbaa664d5
msgid ":ref:`CIRCLE_RATE <CIRCLE_RATE>` = 40"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:241
#: 374f7901d29c4171948f24410e211ace
msgid "You should also set your :ref:`RTL_ALT_M <RTL_ALT_M>` nice and low in case you hit a failsafe, or configure a instant disarm switch on your transmitter for when things go wrong."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vicon-for-nongps-navigation.rst:245
#: 0fabda2e195f4c7eaf19f464fbfcdc04
msgid "To fly in :ref:`Circle mode <circle-mode>` take off in :ref:`Loiter mode <loiter-mode>` and then move so you are 1m from the center of the room, pointing towards the middle of the room. Then switch to Circle mode and the vehicle should start circling, keeping its nose pointed at the center of the circle. You can try pushing up :ref:`CIRCLE_RATE <CIRCLE_RATE>` to higher values (in degrees/second) as you get more confident. The video at the top of this page has :ref:`CIRCLE_RATE <CIRCLE_RATE>` = 150 for a 150 degree/second circle."
msgstr ""
